Two smaller fidelity points: [38;5;10mscanf_i32[0m reads one byte at a time with a single-byte lookahead so leading whitespace is skipped across newlines without over-consuming, and [38;5;10mmain[0m restores the default [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m disposition — the Rust runtime sets it to [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m, which would have exited 0 where the C dies with 141 on an early-closing reader. That signal reset is the only [38;5;10munsafe[0m block in the crate, since disposition isn't reachable from safe [38;5;10mstd[0m.[0m[0m
